{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSVe1yJe5zNAyRdhPYEg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — entity with status field\n- `ShipmentStatus enum:23-27` — CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED values\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` — POST create, GET by id, GET list; uses `ConflictException` for 409 and `ResourceNotFoundException` for 404\n- `InMemoryShipmentRepository.kt` — simple in-memory store with save, findById, existsById\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — `ConflictException` and `ResourceNotFoundException` are the domain error types\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — centralized `ErrorCode` enum\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28` — catches `ApiException` and wraps in `ApiError` envelope\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — uses MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on error codes\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses; `GlobalExceptionHandler` converts them to `ApiError` responses\n2. `ResourceNotFoundException` wraps 404; `ConflictException` wraps 409\n3. Each exception carries an `ErrorCode` enum value\n4. Error responses always use the envelope: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}}`\n5. Tests validate both HTTP status and `error.code` via jsonPath\n6. POST endpoints that create resources return `201 Created`; operations on existing resources should return `200 OK`\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. **`ApiError.kt`** — add new error code for \"cannot confirm cancelled shipment\" (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE or similar)\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`** — add `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** — add tests for all four cases (created→confirmed, already confirmed, cancelled, missing)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Forgetting idempotent behaviour (confirm on already-confirmed must succeed with no change)\n- Breaking existing tests if I accidentally modify Shipment or repository\n- Using wrong HTTP status (should be 200 for successful confirm, 409 for cancelled, 404 for missing)\n- Error code inconsistency\n\n**Open questions:** None; the ticket is unambiguous.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This will be used when confirming a cancelled shipment (409 Conflict).\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`** — Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Takes `shipmentId` as path parameter\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID; if not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)`\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, ...)`\n   - If status is `CREATED`, update it to `CONFIRMED`, save it, and return it\n   - If status is already `CONFIRMED`, return it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - In all success cases, return HTTP 200 OK with the shipment body\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** — Add four tests:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — POST confirm on a newly created shipment, verify status changes and returns 200\n   - `confirm is idempotent on CONFIRMED shipment` — POST confirm twice, second request returns 200 with unchanged shipment\n   - `rejects confirm on CANCELLED shipment with error` — POST confirm on a cancelled shipment, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `rejects confirm on unknown shipment with error` — POST confirm on non-existent ID, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could have added a service layer for the state transition logic, but the existing architecture handles everything in the controller and repository, so adding a service would be unrelated refactoring.\n- Could have used a generic `VALIDATION_FAILED` error code, but the existing pattern creates specific error codes for each business rule (e.g., `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` vs `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`), so a new code is more consistent.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):**\n   - Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n   - Repository: `findById(S-1)` returns Shipment with status CREATED\n   - Controller: creates new Shipment with status CONFIRMED, calls `repository.save(...)`\n   - Response: 200 OK, body is the confirmed shipment\n\n2. **Idempotent path (already CONFIRMED):**\n   - Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n   - Repository: `findById(S-1)` returns Shipment with status CONFIRMED\n   - Controller: detects status is already CONFIRMED, does not call save\n   - Response: 200 OK, body is the unchanged shipment\n\n3. **Conflict path (CANCELLED):**\n   - Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n   - Repository: `findById(S-1)` returns Shipment with status CANCELLED\n   - Controller: detects CANCELLED, throws `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, ...)`\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler: catches it, returns 409 with error envelope\n   - Response: 409 Conflict, body is `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\", \"message\": \"...\"}}`\n\n4. **Not found path:**\n   - Request: `POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm`\n   - Repository: `findById(S-missing)` returns null\n   - Controller: throws `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)`\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler: catches it, returns 404 with error envelope\n   - Response: 404 Not Found, body is `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\", \"message\": \"...\"}}`\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1 covers \"CREATED moves to CONFIRMED\" (acceptance criterion 3)\n- Test 2 covers \"repeated confirm succeeds\" (criterion 5)\n- Test 3 covers \"cancelled shipment is refused\" (criterion 5)\n- Test 4 covers \"unknown id is refused\" (criterion 5)\n- Tests 1-4 together verify error responses are consistent via jsonPath checks on error.code and status codes (criterion 4)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the design. First, I'll add the new error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1380,"cache_read_input_tokens":19357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1380},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62c31993-9d12-411d-b861-3ef8266908e5","uuid":"efc88e7c-84f5-42fa-99f4-7fd0a1bd8c27","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:06:13.024Z","request_id":"req_011CfSVe1bUM9YUj2WD9pyum"}
