{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSVhncEuvDcaNAXVw6aH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass. The verification shows:\n- **Command run:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n- **Result:** BUILD SUCCESS\n- **Tests run:** 17 total (9 in ShipmentControllerTest, which is the 5 existing tests + 4 new confirm tests)\n- **Failures:** 0\n- **Errors:** 0\n\nThe 4 new confirm tests all passed, along with all existing tests.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` succeeded with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass\n3. ✅ **`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it** — Test \"confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED\" validates status changes from CREATED to CONFIRMED and response is 200 OK with the shipment body\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses the same exception classes (`ConflictException`, `ResourceNotFoundException`) and error codes (`SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE`, `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`) as existing endpoints; GlobalExceptionHandler wraps them in the standard `ApiError` envelope\n5. ✅ **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** — Tests \"confirm is idempotent on CONFIRMED shipment\" (succeeds), \"rejects confirm on CANCELLED shipment with error\" (409), \"rejects confirm on unknown shipment with error\" (404)\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — Only modified Kotlin/Spring code; no `pom.xml` changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only touched ShipmentController and ApiError; no refactoring to unrelated files\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`** — Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to ErrorCode enum. This is necessary because the ticket requires rejecting cancelled shipments with 409 Conflict, and the existing error codes don't cover this case.\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`** — Added `confirm()` method that:\n   - Finds the shipment or throws 404\n   - If CANCELLED, throws 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - If CREATED, transitions to CONFIRMED, saves, and returns it\n   - If already CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Returns HTTP 200 OK in success cases (correct for state transition on existing resource)\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** — Added 4 new test methods covering all cases from the requirement:\n   - CREATED → CONFIRMED transition\n   - Idempotent behaviour on already-CONFIRMED\n   - Rejection of CANCELLED with 409 error\n   - Rejection of missing shipment with 404 error\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement:** Add a POST endpoint to confirm shipments that transitions `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status with idempotent behaviour on already-confirmed shipments, 409 rejection for cancelled shipments, and 404 for missing shipments.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `ApiError.kt` — Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code to handle rejection of confirm on cancelled shipments\n- `ShipmentController.kt` — Added `confirm()` POST endpoint at `/{shipmentId}/confirm` with state machine logic\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Added 4 new test methods: confirm CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent on CONFIRMED, reject CANCELLED with 409, reject missing with 404\n\n**Tests:**\n- \"confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED\" — validates status transition from CREATED to CONFIRMED, returns 200 OK with shipment body\n- \"confirm is idempotent on CONFIRMED shipment\" — validates repeated confirm call succeeds, returns 200 OK with unchanged shipment\n- \"rejects confirm on CANCELLED shipment with error\" — validates 409 Conflict with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code\n- \"rejects confirm on unknown shipment with error\" — validates 404 Not Found with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND e